  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat, v0.19.0-era build): \"stepover value doesnt seem to be respected. Going fro 3mm to 25mm stepover doesnt change the tool path one bit.\"\n\nWhat happens: changing an operation's stepover from 3 mm to 25 mm leaves the generated toolpath unchanged.\n\nExpected: the path is regenerated with the new stepover (fewer, wider passes), or the value is refused by name if it is not allowed for the tool (for example larger than the tool diameter). A value that is silently ignored or clamped is wrong either way: the user believes the program cuts with a load it does not cut with.\n\nNot yet known (the report names no operation): which operation and tool. To find out first:\n- which operations read `stepover` at generate, and whether any takes it from somewhere else (a tool default, optimal load, a cached value) and ignores the edited field;\n- whether the edit reaches the operation (the `EditOperationParams` command writes it) and marks the path dirty so it regenerates;\n- whether a clamp (to the tool diameter or a fraction of it) makes 3 mm and 25 mm the same value without telling the user;\n- the trochoidal slot, plain Slot and Adaptive, which the maintainer was testing today (issues 1503, 1504), are the first suspects.\n\nDone means: for every operation that shows a stepover field, a test changes the stepover and asserts that the generated path changes (pass spacing follows the value) or that the value is refused by name; a clamp, where one is right, is shown in the operation's message; an operation that has no use for stepover does not show the field.\n",
